      "demo_description": "",
      "description": "Clone of S10_mit_supercloud_2021-08-11 with the on-site gas turbines removed and primary power supplied by a BC Hydro transmission-voltage grid connection (hydro-dominated system). Same real MIT SuperCloud TX-GAIA GPU job timeline for 2021-08-11 (UTC) and same additive CPU load as S10. All primary energy is grid import, capped at 80 MW at the PCC via grid_import_limit_mw (PROPOSED_HERE: ~125% of the 61.8 MW observed facility peak; covers peak plus the 18 MW BESS charge rate; revised from 60 MW on 2026-10-27, CAV-S11-03). No turbines, solar, or fuel cells. The 18 MW / 14 MWh grid-forming BESS provides ride-through. A 60 MW (6 x 10 MW) diesel block is configured but DISABLED (enabled=false) because the diesel coordinator currently starts on any local gap before grid import is counted; re-enable after a grid-loss gate exists (IMPL-S11-03). No grid-outage event is scripted. grid_import_price_per_mwh 53.74 is BC Hydro RS 1830C (5.374 c/kWh, CAD). BESS initial SoC and diesel sizing are PROPOSED_HERE.",
